WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.780
The husband is very important for you it take time, but I still hope

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.560
you can get married before 30 years old

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.720
-That's not happening

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:24.760
All around the world women face pressure from society and even their own families to live a certain way and fit specific expectations

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:30.059
Whether it's marriage or career related it seems everyone has a thought on how we ought to live

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.660
We partnered with us SK-II, a global skincare brand

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:39.960
that continues to empower women to take control and shape their own destiny as part of their global "Change Destiny" campaign

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.880
Together we explore the pressures women feel to conform to a certain

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:48.760
timeline by inviting mothers and daughters to discuss these very real issues in their own lives

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:52.799
Enjoy the episode and be sure to stick around to the end for more info to share

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.220
Hi everyone, I'm Dr. Jewel. I'm Afrika's mom

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.960
Mom of five and I'm an educator.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.720
My name is Annemarie. I have five children, and I'm a housewife

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.420
My name is Cindy. I have two daughters

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.540
One is Casandra here, and I'm a housewife

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:17.640
I'm Chelsie. I am a travel blogger and a teacher.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.280
My name is Afrika. I am a songwriter and a dancer.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.600
My name is Cassandra. I am a

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:28.320
social media influencer, dancer, and gamer

00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:52.889
I do believe that marriage is an old-fashioned institution

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:56.309
That doesn't mean that you know, it's not important or that it's not relevant

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.439
But I feel like it is dated and it is, you know transforming into something different

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:06.920
I would definitely feel like the reasons for marriage are much different now

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:13.949
than it was before. I don't believe that it is a requirement in life as much.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:19.649
For me it's like the history of marriage started with women literally being sold as if they are property and like that's archaic, you know

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.250
And I just don't agree with that as a concept, but at the same time, you know

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:28.260
I'm a romantic and I believe in love and I believe that if you love someone you should be allowed to marry them

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.340
if that's what you want

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:42.820
My husband and I when we got married we just loved each other and very naturally so we don't have any other

00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:50.759
concern about do we have enough money or do we have any other things we just are very pure... yeah

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.019
Personally, I love I love you mom, but I would not do what you did. I would not do it

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.180
...um if I'm correct um, Mom...

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.180
you got married at 25 and I believe you dated dad for six months -Yes

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.860
-Right? Before that marriage. I personally

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.480
fully believe that before marriage you should be living with that person

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.680
cuz living with someone I feel like it's different than just dating them

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:12.960
-But I don't know

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.260
That whole we're not gonna live together for two years and you ain't put...mm mm

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:17.940
(laughs)

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.260
-See you could die tomorrow

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.340
and I'll just be sitting here with this rent

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:26.940
uh, uh, like there's some assurities in marriage if you want me you got to put up the cost to pay the boss like

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:28.540
Period.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.420
I think you girl- ladies think that um

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:37.320
You're gonna move in with your spouse, right? And then that first year's gonna be bliss if it's the right one

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:42.630
That's not the case. So you move in with someone six month-  'Oh, we're not compatible'

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:47.520
You might have been. If you're married, you're committed to working through life together.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.600
I mean, I don't- Chelsie, I don't know if you're living... are you living with your boyfriend?

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.320
I am and that and that's something that I guess for me is a little bit of a frustration because

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.720
We've been together for almost four years

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.230
I can tell that you know

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:04.290
My siblings that are married and have like a kid on the way or my friends that have kids and are married

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.299
It's their lives and their relationships are taking more seriously than mine is. We are just as committed

00:04:09.299 --> 00:04:14.639
You know, we're monogamous we care about each other. It's a partnership and I just get frustrated that because we're not married

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.630
That means that we're just dating. It's like frivolous. You know what I mean, which it's not

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:24.180
My mom's expectations and goals for me

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:29.820
She wants me to get married and have kids because she thinks that will make me feel fulfilled and happy

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:36.500
Right now, I live with my long-term boyfriend. We don't know if we will ever get married or have children.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:39.380
We're focusing on our careers.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.980
My my passion is traveling and seeing new cultures

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:46.060
That's what makes me happy and brings me joy, and that's what I'm focusing on right now

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.379
My parents are they're kind of wishy-washy

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:05.769
They they respect a little bit of my my wanting to delay my marriage, but on my boyfriend's side of things his mom

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.040
You know, we've been living together for a long time and she didn't really know about it

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.340
I think she kind of did but she wasn't gonna think about it

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.860
She's been calling my boyfriend and every time she's like 'okay, you need to propose.' 'You need to get married you're living together'

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.800
'It's time it's happening' (chuckles)

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.270
I recently uh

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.460
separated from my boyfriend and my dad freaked out

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:30.609
He literally was texting me like he doesn't do drugs. He doesn't gamble. He doesn't drink

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:34.840
He doesn't womanize, he works hard. Like what more do you want?

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:40.820
I didn't know you have the pressure (laughs) of marriage...

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.080
until now

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:49.240
I feel bad. The husband is very important for you. It take time to know this person

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:54.020
So I really don't want to give you any pressure, but I still hope... (laughs)

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.440
you get married before 30 years old

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.480
I love you very much, but that's not happening (laughs)

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:06.980
My mom was the opposite. From the time I was really little she was working full-time. She was never available.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:11.900
I had a friend who I'd go to her house and her mom was there all cute with her cookies. Right?

00:06:11.919 --> 00:06:16.689
And it's like I want that life and it was always get married late and and um

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:23.650
you better continue working in a high-powered job and pay your own bills because if your husband leaves you I guess I just

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:29.320
Bounced and just did the absolute opposite, you know, I did get my degree, but then I was married at 23

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:36.000
I think it's difficult because I think were one of the first generations of when like divorce was common

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:39.130
Like I remember growing up in elementary school

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:43.630
It would be like 75% of the class had parents that were divorced or split up. So I think

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:49.380
We're a lot more, you know nervous. We have a lot more trepidation. We really want to be sure

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:53.260
I mean I get everything that you guys are saying and I understand it

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:58.239
I know what it's like to be in a marriage when you or yourself are not fulfilled and

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:04.820
I wouldn't I wouldn't wish that on anybody. The only challenge if you're constantly like okay. Well, this is great

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.540
And this was two years and the next one would be great. And that was three years

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.770
When do you say?

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:13.060
Okay, right here is where I'm going to build.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.120
But at the same time I mean again, we're not saying date a hundred people

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.580
I know for me personally whenever I'm actually entering it into any relationship

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.940
I do believe this is gonna be the last one.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:28.160
Again, you don't know people a hundred percent until you've dated them until you've taken that time. Time can't be rushed

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.100
My current plan for the future is to establish my career.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:36.200
I'm highly interested in a professional career in songwriting

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.660
I don't have any plans for marriage or kids

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:44.080
Being who I want to be, you know living where I want to live. All those things are important for me right now

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:49.120
By the time I was her age had three kids and I was a mom.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.580
I think womanhood is very powerful

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.780
We literally give life to the world

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:11.500
Have you ever noticed that if- I don't know but I have definitely asked a significant other here or there

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:16.740
or maybe even just a guy friend like 'hey, do you want kids?' you know, and they're all so, like, taken aback

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:19.420
Like, 'I've never been asked that before. Whoa'

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.229
And for women I feel like it's almost expected like you should have a plan

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:29.779
That's the perception we're given especially as women is like you need to be married in order to be happy

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:34.249
You need to have kids in order to be happy or like for your life to mean anything -which not true

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:40.670
I have an aunt who is unmarried and did not have kids and she is a long-term partner that she lives with and

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.440
They travel all the time they of can afford to do what they want

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.200
and they're happy and they are living a good life -Right

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.960
-I made the conscious decision about...mmm

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:56.560
three months ago maybe to get like tubal ligation and basically like tubes tied because I...I don't know

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:02.160
I'm just tired of this whole back-and-forth like 'oh you got to take this birth control' or whatever and like a lot of them don't work for me

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:05.560
When I talk to the doctors, of course, it's their job to like ask you all these questions

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:10.489
'Are you sure?' Blah blah blah and like but it's so interesting they make you sign the paper, but they make you wait 30 days

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:16.730
Again, just in case you change your mind. That's just a decision I made personally because it's just not what I want

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:18.980
I just don't want kids. I never have

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.550
I think it's so funny cuz I think you guys are like breaking their hearts cuz Afrika when you said that you...

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.000
got- did you you get the tubal ligation?

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.000
-No not yet

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.880
-Oh okay cuz know we discussed it

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.160
I'm like getting teary. -Yeah she was over there like yeah  -Honestly

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.880
Like I don't know why I'm sorry, but it's like it's

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.740
What do you know when you're 25? I'm 26

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:44.160
-26

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:50.480
I'm just saying I have friends who made it to like 39 or 40 never wanted kids and then changed their mind

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:57.109
I think it's one of the most amazing things about being a woman is actually carrying a life inside you...you know?

00:09:57.109 --> 00:09:59.100
And and I know you disagree with me

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:03.560
How do you young people feel when you hear her saying she wants tubal ligation?

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:07.909
I was really surprised by that. Um I support you absolutely

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.149
Um but that's definitely not what I would want for myself

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:16.040
It's something I wouldn't do because I'm still very uncertain, it changes everyday

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:19.490
So for you to have the courage to do it, I believe that you are

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.700
all-knowing and that you really believe in it.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:26.320
You know, we have five kids. My middle daughter is like the opposite of me

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:28.360
She's in an all-male business

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:35.380
high-powered job and then I talked to her about kids and having you know having a family getting married and

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.780
and she blows me off

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:44.020
I really try to hold back from being- like pushing my opinions on people, but I do. You know my daughter

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:47.810
I'm like 'You really need to have at least one child just to experience it'

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:48.230
-Well

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.910
I didn't know if you did it or not

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:54.469
Cuz I just had to let it just at the end of the day it's your body. It's your decision

00:10:54.469 --> 00:10:59.040
I would never say you have to have a child. It was very disappointing and hurtful for me though

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.100
I feel that having children and

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:04.260
bringing life is like the most natural thing like...

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:08.140
- So for me um my mom had me really young and uh

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:09.750
I watched her give up

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.720
Everything, you know, to be a mother and to raise me and she was a single mom for a while

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:18.080
Um in a selfish way, part of me is like, 'I don't know if I can do that...

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.300
to the level she did

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:26.960
And I feel bad because I- you knows part of me is like 'do I owe her a grandchild'

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:28.900
because of what she did for me, you know what I mean?

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:31.500
do I owe her.. do I owe her that?

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.500
If I think if you have a

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:37.600
marriage and have a children one day of you really sick and

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.279
parents are not here and

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.560
someone can take care of you

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:43.380
-I agree

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:48.480
but I feel like there's so much more that I need to learn and I'm just now learning

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:51.880
Like it's scaring me how some people that I know who are getting married

00:11:51.889 --> 00:11:53.899
you know don't know how to do their taxes and

00:11:53.999 --> 00:11:57.769
Everything's just kind of taken care of and that that can be a nice thing

00:11:57.769 --> 00:12:00.760
But for me, I very much want to be able to take care of myself

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:07.840
I also know myself and I'm a very social person. If I am on my deathbed with whatever cancer it may be at that point

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.269
I feel like I would have no trouble having people who care about me

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.640
surrounding me

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.660
I got married when I was 25

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:24.620
Even though she has a lot of friends. I think the family is the most important

00:12:25.319 --> 00:12:30.409
-I would love to have children in the future. I just don't know if that's like my top priority right now

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:36.260
The personal goal of mine to build my Chinese lion dance team and to

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.180
uh pursue the endeavors that I've started

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:47.660
-Go ahead (laughs)

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.000
-Am I the only one?

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:54.640
(sighs)

00:12:54.940 --> 00:13:00.700
It's embarrassing to admit but it's just I just feel like, you know, I'm not like my husband

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:01.880
And

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:05.560
The way we've set up our family has worked for us

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.200
You know what? I'm okay bringing- making him dinner every night

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.720
I'm okay for him um

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.640
you know paying the bills

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:13.620
And

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:17.360
You know, I was really okay having children and you know

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:22.279
I think children do better when a mom is at home and she takes on that traditional role

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:24.540
Don't hate me ladies

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:26.540
-We don't hate you (laughs)

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.300
-We love you. You're fine

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:33.380
It's just it's not a popular choice right? It's not a popular thought

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:35.380
-But I think it's a spectrum. Right?

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:39.220
Because I definitely believe in letting a man be a man, but he can cook too

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:40.440
There's nothing wrong with that

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:46.070
Who really has the right to tell somebody 'this is what real womanhood is' or 'this is what real manhood is'

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:49.909
somebody could say, you know, I wasn't a good mom for taking my kids down to

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:55.070
the university twice a week because I needed to finish my masters

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:57.900
But I did that so that I could be a better mom to them

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.900
My boyfriend and I have a pretty interesting situation

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:06.840
He's he's from a pretty traditional family, but I'm crazy crazy independent

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:11.930
I'm I'm like the the financier of a lot of the relationship and a lot of times he cooks and

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:16.249
We have that flipped, but we've made it work

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:21.560
I'm on this whole thing right now where I separated from my boyfriend because I was like I need to live on my own

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.740
for a while because I found myself changing

00:14:24.779 --> 00:14:26.779
within the relationship and

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:31.940
Losing my independence to the point where I felt like I couldn't do things

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:33.040
When we first got married

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:38.560
we fell into those roles, you know, and so my husband hasn't cooked dinner for us

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.560
for like 28 years

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:44.460
I'm not up on our finances. He pays all the bills

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:50.720
I've given all that over to him out of you know in my early 20s it's worked for us

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:54.470
So, I don't know if it's a bad thing? You know, what if he wasn't supportive

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:57.470
I probably couldn't be that kind of wife or couldn't do that, right?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:02.809
But I did struggle with guilt a little bit that I've kind of given that over to my husband all this time

00:15:02.809 --> 00:15:05.440
You know, and I've kind of gotten to a safe place

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:07.340
umm

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:09.780
But maybe...maybe that's gonna change

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.120
-Okay girlfriend

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.640
Damn...go get your money girl

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.140
I got married at 23

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:21.280
A year and half later I was pregnant with my first of five

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:23.240
I love having a big family

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:26.160
There's this built-in community and support for one another

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:33.460
My middle daughter's this beautiful girl and she's so independent and all over the place and traveling all over by herself

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:34.720
I want her to be safe

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:37.420
I want her to be happy. I'd love for her to get married

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:40.460
She met a wonderful man, and she seems really happy.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:16:03.620
I am so scared despite everything that I say. I'm so scared of disappointing you mom and dad. Oh, I already know I've disappointed dad

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.480
-You didn't disappointed to us

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:13.300
Actually, I knew you worked very very hard. You really work very hard. So I think you have the talent

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:16.240
For your dream. - Thanks mom.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.780
- I think for me um I've risked so much

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:24.180
I want my kids to know that risk is okay... that a calculated risk is okay

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:32.640
Um and so I can't fail because I know they're looking at me and if they have any dreams in their hearts

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:38.090
And I give up our mine... How can I ever say something to them, you know?

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.540
Me personally, I guess I don't really think about it because

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:48.360
Both of my parents are probably the best role models for like you do what you want to do, you know

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:53.809
Like my dad, he loved trucks and trains since he was a kid and so I became a truck driver. My mom

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:56.390
she discovered West African dance when she was 18

00:16:56.390 --> 00:17:02.294
And so that's what she did she became a dancer and then people maybe thought they were crazy, but they did it anyway

00:17:02.294 --> 00:17:04.940
-Of course I am little scared of disappointing my mom

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:09.950
but I think overall I think I think she's proud and she knows you know that

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:15.349
everything that I do is with good intent and I think if I choose not to get married to have kids

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:17.100
I think that'll be another painful thing for her

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:21.200
But she'll understand because she loves me and she knows I'm doing what's best for me

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:26.540
- I think there is a part of Rachel, my middle daughter, that um I think know

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:32.239
she doesn't want to disappoint me. She was engaged for a long time to it to a guy she met when she was 18

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:33.660
and

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:37.100
It wasn't right, she wasn't happy, she wasn't glowing

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:41.100
she was so worried about disappointing me because I had already paid for the venue

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:44.060
that she was gonna go through with the wedding

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:47.480
so I took her for a walk on the beach, and I said 'Rachel

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.120
I don't care. You could be, you can have the flowers in hand

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.220
In the white dress. Ready to walk down the aisle. And you could say

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:57.980
Mommy take me away and I would put you in the car and you wouldn't have to face anything at all'

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:03.320
I think as moms, we just want the best for you guys. We just want you to be fulfilled and happy

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:06.480
and she doesn't want you to have any regrets in life

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.680
She doesn't want you to look back when you're our age and go

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:14.620
'Damn I wish I had done it differently' or 'I wish I had made this decision, you know, make sure that you're doing

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:18.380
what's gonna be right for you. Not just now but for you know, 20 years from now

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:28.660
-Yay (claps)

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.080
-That's all of us (laughs)

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:33.920
-You know as a mom we really love you guys and no matter what you do

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.600
We love you period.

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:41.080
It's not about these rigid rules and regulations and 'you must this' and the timeline and the ticking clock

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:44.140
It's about I love you. No matter what.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.040
It's it's a different world now and

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.720
So we can't expect you to be the same

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:55.040
Women that are this- that fall into the same rules that maybe I did when I was 22. It's opened my mind

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.390
So I'm very grateful for that

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:57.520
So thank you

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:03.420
And it's good to hear from people's perspective people who have gone the more traditional route of getting married and having kids and

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.920
To see you fulfilled. That's really great

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:10.620
I think today is nice too to have an open and honest communication

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:15.200
with some other mothers that I think my mom would agree with so it was really nice to maybe

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.630
Hear the words that she would want to say to me

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:22.309
But she doesn't feel right saying to me and I really appreciated hearing that and it's helped me

00:19:22.309 --> 00:19:24.080
I don't know maybe rethink some things

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:28.720
- I definitely know that sometimes when my parents tell me something I kind of blow it off

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:32.659
It's not that they'll never get it, but it's just um we come from two

00:19:33.299 --> 00:19:37.459
completely different times. You know, the world is changing. We're all changing

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:38.840
We're always changing

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:43.020
- Probably I gave Cassandra a lot of pressure. I think so. Yeah

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:44.220
-It's okay

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:50.360
I didn't do that on purpose. I want to communicate with you more. I hope to know

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:58.040
anything in your deep in your mind and you can ask me anything you want to from now on

00:19:58.820 --> 00:19:59.460
Okay?

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.480
-Thanks mom

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:02.440
-Thank you

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:07.960
-I just want to see her happy (laughs)

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:13.900
I would want to see her just continue to know that those things that are in her heart

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:19.040
Are valid, are important and that the world meets them and needs her

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:22.180
-The challenges that young women have today are very different

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:27.720
When I was younger there was, you know a few paths that I could take, but now

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:30.080
You know women can do anything.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:35.360
-You know me not being a mom myself, it's hard for me to realize the reasoning behind

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:37.120
my mom's opinions

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:41.659
I know she only has my best interests in mind and that's what she wants

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:46.909
- Despite the generation time gap, at the end of the day, we all have the same goals

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:50.080
We all want to feel fulfilled and live a happy life

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.440
We're just taking different paths to get there

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.200
Thank you so much everyone for watching

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:02.320
This is a topic that's really close to our hearts

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:05.280
and it was an absolute privilege to have all these women come in and

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.400
open their lives up to us and be a part of this discussion

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:10.500
Absolutely and we want to send a huge shout out to SK-II. Thank you so much

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:15.849
They made this video possible and they were super supportive. So we highly recommend that you guys check out #timelines

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:18.819
It's this awesome docu-series that SK-II did with Katie Couric

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:22.209
It explores the pressures put on women around the world by like

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:27.800
society and their families but also shows amazing stories of women who are following their dreams and creating their own destiny

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.380
And we hope you guys do the same

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:34.599
Our team here at Jubilee loved this series and we know that our audience will too. Until next time guys. See ya!

